WEBVTT

00:01.360 --> 00:03.220
<i>How do you do?</i>

00:03.220 --> 00:04.840
<i>I am the Empress.</i>

00:04.840 --> 00:07.390
I have no clue what 
that's supposed to mean.

00:07.390 --> 00:09.600
I see why she'd get attention, though.

00:09.600 --> 00:11.320
She looks exactly like you.

00:11.320 --> 00:14.100
No wonder they call her a doppelgänger.

00:15.090 --> 00:18.370
<i>Are you watching closely, fake me?</i>

00:18.700 --> 00:22.880
<i>I want to take back the name of 
Saionji Sarasa that you stole from me.</i>

00:23.330 --> 00:26.120
<i>So why don't we play a game?</i>

00:26.120 --> 00:27.180
Huh?

00:27.180 --> 00:27.880
A game?

00:28.170 --> 00:32.260
<i>The setting will be the 
May Inter-Academy Battle, ASTRAL.</i>

00:32.260 --> 00:35.920
<i>And to win, you have to 
defeat Shinohara Hiroto.</i>

00:35.920 --> 00:36.500
Huh?

00:35.920 --> 00:36.500
Huh?!

00:38.550 --> 00:42.280
<i>Whoever beats him gets 
to be the real Saionji Sarasa.</i>

00:42.280 --> 00:47.620
<i>If I win, you have to surrender 
your Saionji Sarasa account to me.</i>

00:47.620 --> 00:51.070
<i>If you win, you can be the true Empress.</i>

00:51.070 --> 00:55.040
<i>If Shinohara Hiroto wins, I'll let him
 decide what he does with me.</i>

00:55.040 --> 00:59.350
<i>But don't forget that I look 
exactly like you right now.</i>

00:59.350 --> 01:03.910
<i>So if you refuse, I might just have 
to strip to deal with the stress.</i>

01:03.910 --> 01:04.900
What?!

01:03.910 --> 01:04.900
Ah!

01:05.190 --> 01:12.050
<i>Thousands of people might see me doing 
all sorts of things to make myself feel good.</i>

01:14.260 --> 01:16.750
<i>I hope you'll give me the right answer.</i>

01:20.560 --> 01:22.690
Aw, damn it!

01:23.500 --> 01:25.670
What the hell <i>is</i> this?!

01:25.670 --> 01:28.260
H-Hey, try to calm down.

01:29.970 --> 01:30.900
Listen.

01:31.840 --> 01:34.410
Kurahashi must be involved in this.

01:34.680 --> 01:35.930
Good point.

01:35.930 --> 01:40.670
Kurahashi knows I helped you out 
in the All-Campus Elimination Battle.

01:41.610 --> 01:45.570
He might have realized 
you and I aren't actually rivals.

01:45.570 --> 01:49.560
So he's coming after both of us
this time, I guess?

01:49.560 --> 01:53.740
Tch. That scumbag Kurahashi 
is constantly screwing with us.

03:25.060 --> 03:28.150
I'm begging you! Please help us, Kagaya-san!

03:25.100 --> 03:30.100
Good Night

03:28.400 --> 03:30.380
Uh, so, basically...

03:30.690 --> 03:34.660
You need to kill it as the commander 
so your teammates won't uncover your lie,

03:34.660 --> 03:36.750
while taking out three other leaders

03:36.750 --> 03:39.890
and preparing to fight 
a super dangerous doppelgänger?

03:39.890 --> 03:41.030
Pretty much.

03:41.030 --> 03:43.660
You're a real slave driver, Hiro-kyun.

03:43.660 --> 03:46.660
Also, he must be victorious in ASTRAL.

03:46.910 --> 03:51.870
Members of teams who place sixth or lower 
all have one Star taken away from them.

03:51.870 --> 03:54.730
If I lose a star, I'm done for.

03:57.050 --> 04:00.790
In addition, a new rule has 
just been posted on Libra.

04:02.390 --> 04:04.150
It involves a voting system.

04:04.150 --> 04:08.760
Students on the island all get to vote
 to predict the event's winners.

04:05.010 --> 04:09.180
Support Rating

04:09.190 --> 04:13.200
And those support ratings have an effect
 on players' movement values?

04:13.200 --> 04:16.180
But that only comes into 
play in the second half.

04:16.180 --> 04:19.690
In the first half, positions and abilities
 will decide who wins battles.

04:20.380 --> 04:23.820
The Company can access the 
servers to borrow some data,

04:23.820 --> 04:27.950
then I can send it on to you 
in real time. That sound okay?

04:28.290 --> 04:29.160
Yeah!

04:29.160 --> 04:32.440
Master, what will you do 
with your ability settings?

04:32.440 --> 04:33.200
Oh, right.

04:33.210 --> 04:37.710
<i>Black Wings</i>

04:33.210 --> 04:37.710
Available to the holder of the Indigo Star.

04:33.210 --> 04:37.710
This ability enhances performances,
allowing the user to employ things
like smoke and sound effects on stage.
 It also allows the user to transmit their 
voice far away.

04:33.210 --> 04:37.710
Add

04:33.450 --> 04:37.610
In the first slot, I'll use the 
Indigo Star's ability, Black Wings.

04:37.610 --> 04:40.420
In the second, I'll use the 
Green Star's Predict Movement.

04:37.710 --> 04:43.720
<i>Predict Movement</i>

04:37.710 --> 04:43.720
Available to the holder of the Green Star.

04:37.710 --> 04:43.720
A special ability that applies the 
sensory effect of the special 
Green Star to largely alter the 
abilities exhibited by whoever holds it.

04:37.710 --> 04:43.720
Add

04:40.420 --> 04:43.710
And in the third... 
I need to think about it some more.

04:44.060 --> 04:45.720
What are you going to use, Himeji?

04:46.740 --> 04:49.470
I will use an ability 
I've saved for a special occasion.

04:49.470 --> 04:50.860
A special occasion?

04:50.860 --> 04:51.940
Yes.

04:51.940 --> 04:55.850
An assist ability that allows 
players to exchange one ability.

04:56.240 --> 04:57.730
It is called Replacement.

04:56.440 --> 05:01.480
Replacement

04:57.730 --> 05:01.490
It is very expensive, so I will have 
the Company procure it for me.

05:01.870 --> 05:04.250
But does it not sound potentially useful?

05:04.250 --> 05:05.580
Yeah.

05:08.870 --> 05:12.880
<i>Roger. Sounds like Eimei 
Academy's all ready to go, too.</i>

05:12.880 --> 05:15.850
Yeah. I guess that's where we're at now.

05:15.850 --> 05:18.290
<i>This whole thing is kind 
of depressing, though.</i>

05:18.290 --> 05:18.860
Huh?

05:18.860 --> 05:23.030
All the Ouka kids keep staring 
at me with stars in their eyes.

05:23.030 --> 05:25.210
Yeah, but that's normal, right?

05:25.210 --> 05:27.680
I'll be with them all the time 
during the event.

05:27.680 --> 05:30.010
The only time I'll get 
to myself is when I'm asleep.

05:30.460 --> 05:33.020
And I won't get to talk to you.

05:33.330 --> 05:34.190
Huh?

05:35.030 --> 05:38.730
<i>I-I'm not saying I'm desperate to see you!</i>

05:38.730 --> 05:41.230
<i>I just won't have anyone 
to blow off steam with!</i>

05:42.150 --> 05:43.150
It's fine.

05:44.760 --> 05:46.590
I didn't say anything.

05:48.260 --> 05:50.150
Don't lose, Saionji.

05:50.460 --> 05:51.180
Hmph.

05:52.680 --> 05:55.530
The Empress won't lose so easily.

05:55.530 --> 05:58.910
Good. I'm rooting for you. Good night.

05:58.910 --> 06:00.680
<i>Yeah, good night.</i>

06:06.410 --> 06:08.800
Hello? Yeah, it's me.

06:09.110 --> 06:11.230
I want you to help me with something.

06:15.180 --> 06:18.140
ASTRAL First Day: Morning

06:17.140 --> 06:19.590
This is where it's being held?

06:21.520 --> 06:23.900
Good meow-ning, everyone!

06:23.900 --> 06:26.440
I'm Kazami Suzuran from Libra, meow!

06:26.440 --> 06:29.240
The weather's clear and 
maybe even a little hot right now!

06:29.570 --> 06:34.230
But now we're gonna play a game <i>so</i> hot,
 you might get burnt just watching it, meow!

06:34.610 --> 06:37.970
Okay, everyone! Come with me, meow!

06:38.750 --> 06:43.260
The entire game will be held 
in augmented reality, meow.

06:44.600 --> 06:46.880
This is incredible.

06:46.880 --> 06:49.660
Isn't this, like, super high resolution?

06:50.510 --> 06:51.830
Wow.

06:57.770 --> 06:59.560
<i>ASTRAL is beginning.</i>

07:00.600 --> 07:05.150
<i>Teams from all academies, please stand
 at your designated starting points.</i>

07:02.350 --> 07:07.570
Soldier

07:02.350 --> 07:07.570
Asamiya Nanase

07:02.350 --> 07:07.570
Mage

07:02.350 --> 07:07.570
Enomoto Shinji

07:02.350 --> 07:07.570
Commander

07:02.350 --> 07:07.570
Shinohara Hiroto

07:02.350 --> 07:07.570
Guardian

07:02.350 --> 07:07.570
Himeji Shirayuki

07:02.350 --> 07:07.570
Spy

07:02.350 --> 07:07.570
Akizuki Noa

07:06.630 --> 07:09.490
All right. Let's begin.

07:09.490 --> 07:11.030
Guys, do you see that?

07:12.180 --> 07:14.650
That's our first base.

07:17.770 --> 07:21.470
And over there is a neutral base.

07:22.040 --> 07:25.260
We have to take control of it
 to expand our area.

07:25.260 --> 07:27.220
Shall we try it out?

07:27.220 --> 07:28.060
Sure.

07:29.000 --> 07:33.160
This is so exciting. It feels like we're 
doing something naughty, Hiroto-kun.

07:33.160 --> 07:35.510
No, it doesn't. What are you talking about?

07:37.690 --> 07:40.740
Okay, this is the neutral area.

07:40.740 --> 07:42.750
All right. Here I go.

