08:06.700 --> 08:09.020
Himeji, your movement value is 9, right?

08:09.020 --> 08:13.540
Yes. And since the Freeze Time 
counter displayed 90 seconds,

08:13.540 --> 08:16.800
it seems it takes 10 times your 
movement value to occupy a space.

08:16.800 --> 08:19.270
That would really slow us down.

08:19.590 --> 08:24.740
No, when it comes to Freeze Time, 
losing our abilities is the bigger problem.

08:25.200 --> 08:30.460
In battle, if you're attacked after using 
an ability, you might not be able to evade.

08:30.460 --> 08:33.420
Then we should check out
 that Freeze Time, too.

08:33.420 --> 08:37.280
Ooh, me! I'll try that out for you.

08:39.400 --> 08:41.320
I'll use Numerical Adjustment.

08:39.410 --> 08:41.330
Ability

08:39.410 --> 08:41.330
Numerical
\hAdjustment

08:41.320 --> 08:44.830
I'll max out your interest 
in me, Hiroto-kun.

08:45.250 --> 08:47.820
That won't actually test 
your ability, though.

08:47.830 --> 08:55.550
Freeze Time

