09:09.500 --> 09:14.080
When you're in your own area, it looks 
like your movement value drops by 2.

09:14.770 --> 09:19.030
So the more you expand your area, the more 
range you have to move around effectively.

09:19.030 --> 09:21.070
Yeah, exactly right.

09:21.070 --> 09:25.670
Huh. I guess he isn't just a 
good-for-nothing loudmouth.

09:25.670 --> 09:28.660
I went ahead and searched 
nearby with my ability.

09:29.240 --> 09:32.920
I know where the bases are, so that 
should make our plan a little easier.

09:30.710 --> 09:32.920
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

09:30.710 --> 09:32.920
Information Control EX {情報統制EX}

09:32.920 --> 09:35.790
So I guess we need to start capturing bases.

09:35.790 --> 09:39.430
Yeah. There are two nearby,
one to the north, one to the east.

09:39.430 --> 09:41.520
If we're moving, east is our only option.

09:41.940 --> 09:44.880
From what I can see, 
base placement isn't random.

09:44.880 --> 09:47.980
They're likely spaced relatively 
equally for a better show.

09:47.980 --> 09:52.940
With that in mind, we can assume 
there are some bases off the map, too.

09:53.260 --> 09:59.450
Therefore, I think the most efficient way 
to expand our area is by moving east.

09:59.450 --> 10:04.680
Guess so. Also, spells are released 
from bases at regular intervals.

10:05.120 --> 10:07.820
But we can't use them like that yet.

