10:11.840 --> 10:14.840
Conceal

10:15.210 --> 10:17.650
So you have to pay 
attention to what you have.

10:17.650 --> 10:18.730
Mm-hmm.

10:18.730 --> 10:23.360
But I guess we can just pick whatever to 
start with. I'm gonna go with this one.

10:23.360 --> 10:26.030
Hey, no fair, Noa-chi!

10:26.030 --> 10:27.160
I wanna pick, too!

10:28.140 --> 10:31.270
How long do you think the
Freeze Time is for spells?

10:31.270 --> 10:33.280
I can test that out!

10:33.540 --> 10:35.640
I'll try taking a swing at you, Shinji.

10:35.640 --> 10:38.530
Wait, Nanase. You're testing
 a blade out on a friend?

10:38.530 --> 10:42.370
What? You'd love to be 
murdered by a cute girl.

10:42.370 --> 10:46.970
I can't dispute your logic, but if it's you, 
Nanase, the premise doesn't hold.

10:46.970 --> 10:48.830
Now I really <i>will</i> kill you.

10:48.090 --> 10:48.830
Huh?

10:48.830 --> 10:51.240
Hey, Akizuki. Where'd Himeji go?

10:51.650 --> 10:52.640
Huh?

10:55.620 --> 10:56.630
Guess who.

10:57.350 --> 10:59.520
Himeji, is that you?

11:00.900 --> 11:05.500
Yes. I decided to try out the Conceal spell.

11:05.510 --> 11:12.270
Freeze Time

11:05.840 --> 11:10.000
The displayed Freeze Time is 18 seconds,
 so it is twice the movement value.

11:10.000 --> 11:12.270
O-Oh, no kidding.

11:12.670 --> 11:17.020
Um, Master... Have I done something wrong?

11:17.290 --> 11:19.400
Wow, a sword!

11:17.330 --> 11:19.320
I think I'm the one in the wrong.

11:18.160 --> 11:19.400
Stop that.

11:19.320 --> 11:20.090
Huh?

11:19.400 --> 11:21.400
I said the premise doesn't hold.

11:21.400 --> 11:23.230
Look up "premise" in a dictionary.

11:21.400 --> 11:23.230
Get killed by a cute girl!

11:23.240 --> 11:25.200
First Day: Finished

11:25.200 --> 11:27.200
Team with the most held areas:
District 3's Ouka Academy

11:25.200 --> 11:27.200
spaces

11:27.200 --> 11:30.000
Team with the most supporting votes:
District 4's Eimei Academy

11:35.970 --> 11:38.710
Good to see you again, Shinohara Hiroto.

11:39.340 --> 11:43.410
I should thank you for slithering out
 in front of me like this,

11:43.410 --> 11:46.350
and giving me an opportunity 
to get my revenge.

11:46.350 --> 11:49.180
I didn't come here to see you, you know.

11:49.180 --> 11:51.650
Act smug while you can.

11:51.650 --> 11:54.710
Our team from Otowa will 
rightly crush your Eimei antics.

11:54.710 --> 11:56.730
Duly look forward to that.

12:00.790 --> 12:02.820
District 8's Otowa Academy.

12:02.820 --> 12:06.240
Their team is made up of members 
of the group Kugasaki-sama leads,

12:06.240 --> 12:07.820
the Self-Made Holy Knight Brigade.

12:09.130 --> 12:12.550
Kugasaki-sama possesses 
infectious charisma,

12:12.550 --> 12:15.200
and I think his team may be 
one of our greatest threats.

12:16.120 --> 12:17.500
How about the other teams?

12:17.500 --> 12:18.590
Right.

12:18.590 --> 12:21.380
District 7's Shinra High School.

12:21.670 --> 12:26.140
The school traditionally has a very hostile 
culture, and they placed third last year.

12:26.140 --> 12:29.380
Their player to watch out for
 is Kirigaya Touya-sama.

12:29.380 --> 12:32.770
He's a Six Star who believes in 
doing whatever is necessary to win.

12:33.110 --> 12:34.940
His nickname is the "Absolute Monarch."

12:34.940 --> 12:36.850
I hear that when you play him...

12:37.490 --> 12:42.230
...he tries to overwhelm you with moves 
and bombard you with violent tactics.

12:42.230 --> 12:46.280
I know several people who just gave up 
and left the island after playing him.

12:46.550 --> 12:47.800
<i>Are you serious?</i>

12:47.800 --> 12:49.040
By the way...

12:49.370 --> 12:50.400
Huh?

12:50.400 --> 12:52.550
The girl over there is serious trouble.

12:52.550 --> 12:57.480
Kururugi Senri from District 16. 
She's the leader of Tsuyuri Girls' Academy.

12:57.480 --> 12:59.410
She's some kind of monster.

12:59.780 --> 13:03.480
If you bump into her, 
I recommend running away.

13:03.480 --> 13:05.040
But why?

13:05.310 --> 13:08.420
Kururugi-sama's ability 
is absolutely nefarious.

13:08.840 --> 13:10.550
It's called One-Shot Kill.

13:11.030 --> 13:15.550
If the conditions are met, that ability can 
send players to their grave in one attack.

13:16.930 --> 13:18.690
That vicious nature...

13:19.590 --> 13:23.050
has earned her the 
nickname of "Demon Maiden."

13:24.840 --> 13:27.140
Thanks very much for the compliment.

13:28.260 --> 13:33.700
But isn't it a bit rude of you? 
Talking about someone behind their back.

13:33.700 --> 13:36.700
<i>Yikes, yikes, yikes! 
Why's she carrying around a wooden sword?</i>

13:37.220 --> 13:42.980
From what I heard, you have 
some reality-transcending ability

13:42.980 --> 13:45.960
that lets you find winning 
strategies against any opponent.

13:46.610 --> 13:49.340
You graduated from an
 American college at five,

13:49.340 --> 13:53.060
and an organization put you through
inhumane training to develop these skills.

13:53.060 --> 13:54.480
That's what I heard.

13:54.760 --> 13:57.900
Wait. Where's that information from?

13:57.900 --> 13:59.990
From a Libra article, obviously.

13:59.990 --> 14:01.730
<i>Kazami again.</i>

14:02.330 --> 14:07.240
But it doesn't matter. No matter 
how strong you are, Tsuyuri will win.

14:10.110 --> 14:12.990
The rest of your team 
looks to be full of holes, too.

14:17.660 --> 14:21.620
And finally, the player we have to 
be most cautious of this time around

14:21.620 --> 14:24.050
is surely that doppelgänger.

14:25.210 --> 14:28.380
Due to the scandal with former 
headmaster Kurahashi Mikado,

14:28.380 --> 14:33.180
Seijo Academy cannot participate, and she 
has snuck into the event by taking their slot.

14:33.620 --> 14:38.130
She is a scoundrel, picking a fight with 
the Empress and getting you involved.

14:38.130 --> 14:39.620
We must be wary.

14:43.760 --> 14:45.760
Thanks for the meal.

14:46.070 --> 14:48.410
So, how are we splitting the rooms?

14:48.410 --> 14:51.040
I think I should stay with Hiroto-kun.

14:52.540 --> 14:53.950
What a foolish question.

14:53.950 --> 14:58.040
As long as I'm not sharing with Nanase,
 I have no preference.

14:58.040 --> 15:01.990
What a sneaky way of saying you <i>do</i> have one.
 You just don't wanna room with me, huh?

15:01.990 --> 15:05.400
So you're okay sharing with another girl?

15:05.400 --> 15:07.290
I didn't say anything of the sort.

15:07.600 --> 15:12.270
Regardless, it has been decided 
that Master and I will share a room,

15:12.270 --> 15:16.800
so if Akizuki-sama joins us, 
would you two not be together?

15:16.810 --> 15:20.910
Wait! No way! I can't even imagine 
staying in a room with Shinji!

15:20.910 --> 15:24.770
Agreed. How could I sleep next to 
a girl who tosses and turns so much?

15:24.770 --> 15:26.940
That was back in grade school!

15:26.940 --> 15:30.210
You guys slept in the same room 
when you were in grade school?

15:32.970 --> 15:37.480
Hiroto-kun! You can squeeze me 
like a full-body pillow, okay?

15:37.480 --> 15:41.130
I cannot let you have such 
a crucial role, Akizuki-sama.

15:42.290 --> 15:45.290
Let me set you idiots straight.

15:46.040 --> 15:48.540
Boys and girls...

15:48.900 --> 15:50.300
sleep in separate rooms!

15:50.300 --> 15:51.430
Aw.

15:56.110 --> 15:58.390
Oh, dang. I must have dozed off.

15:59.680 --> 16:00.640
A futon?

16:05.140 --> 16:07.290
Are you actually a nice guy, Enomoto?

16:08.500 --> 16:09.940
Maybe I'll take a bath.

16:10.190 --> 16:12.700
Men's Bath

16:12.700 --> 16:14.700
Main Bath

16:14.700 --> 16:14.820
Main Bath

16:14.820 --> 16:14.950
Main Bath

16:15.500 --> 16:16.330
Oh?

16:19.320 --> 16:20.510
Hm?

16:21.580 --> 16:23.710
Come on.

16:24.800 --> 16:28.470
If that's how it is, I'll have 
to use my secret power.

16:29.500 --> 16:30.350
Here.

16:30.350 --> 16:30.970
Huh?

16:31.280 --> 16:33.580
Jeez. Jumping's dangerous, you know.

16:34.260 --> 16:35.190
See you.

16:35.980 --> 16:37.090
Um...

16:37.090 --> 16:37.790
Hm?

16:38.700 --> 16:42.350
Thank you, uh, very much?

16:42.350 --> 16:44.140
Was that a question?

16:45.050 --> 16:50.530
I don't know what might happen next,
 so I thought I shouldn't act too familiar.

16:50.530 --> 16:52.360
Wow, you sure are cautious.

16:52.710 --> 16:54.620
But what are you doing here?

16:54.970 --> 16:58.360
What? You mean, like, my raison d'être?

16:58.360 --> 17:02.280
Raison... Uh, I don't know about that.

17:02.280 --> 17:05.140
But this place is totally 
booked for our event.

17:05.140 --> 17:08.750
Aren't you in middle school? 
You can't be a player, then.

17:08.750 --> 17:12.150
Um, actually, I am sort of a participant.

17:12.150 --> 17:18.100
My big sister works for Libra and 
she asked me to be in the MTCG.

17:18.100 --> 17:18.870
See?

17:19.490 --> 17:20.780
<i>A room key?</i>

17:21.700 --> 17:26.890
<i>MTCG. The optional game that's being 
held at the same time as ASTRAL?</i>

17:27.200 --> 17:29.100
Can you get back to your room alone?

17:29.100 --> 17:31.100
Mm-hmm. But...

17:31.100 --> 17:31.720
Hm?

17:32.020 --> 17:34.470
Hey, your eye.

17:34.470 --> 17:35.160
Hm?

17:35.640 --> 17:37.010
Oh, this is a colored con—

17:37.440 --> 17:40.770
Um, I mean, it's because I'm the chosen one.

17:40.770 --> 17:43.350
That's why my eye color is so cool.

17:43.350 --> 17:46.780
See? Look, I have heterochromia! Impressed?

17:47.990 --> 17:49.300
Yeah, I'm impressed.

17:49.640 --> 17:51.120
You are?

17:51.120 --> 17:57.640
Hey, listen, listen. My right eye's magical,
so I can see way into the past and future!

17:57.640 --> 18:01.620
I can tell you're a 
special person, too, mister.

18:02.860 --> 18:05.800
Huh. Sounds like a pretty 
overactive magic eye.

18:06.320 --> 18:07.250
See you later.

18:07.250 --> 18:08.150
H-Hey.

18:09.460 --> 18:13.090
Can't you come play with me, mister?

18:13.090 --> 18:13.970
Huh?

18:15.500 --> 18:16.890
You're so great, mister!

18:17.840 --> 18:19.400
You're so strong, mister!

18:19.980 --> 18:21.920
You're so fast, mister!

18:22.700 --> 18:24.230
Wow.

18:24.230 --> 18:28.540
This little one would be a perfect familiar
for someone as powerful as me, right?

18:28.960 --> 18:33.050
Okay, Lloyd. Look this way
 and gaze into my eye.

18:33.050 --> 18:36.880
I'll teach you who you belong to now.

18:36.880 --> 18:38.420
You already gave it a name?

18:41.170 --> 18:43.560
Wow! Awesome! Awesome!

18:43.560 --> 18:46.150
You're so awesome, mister! Good job!

18:46.500 --> 18:47.550
You're welcome.

18:49.390 --> 18:51.190
Here. Your precious Lloyd.

18:51.190 --> 18:55.020
Yay! Thank you, mister!

18:59.350 --> 19:00.820
So sleepy.

19:01.160 --> 19:03.070
Huh? Hey now.

19:08.570 --> 19:11.950
Room 415... Room 415...

19:11.950 --> 19:12.340
Oh.

19:16.810 --> 19:18.430
There you go.

19:23.590 --> 19:26.100
You've got to eat better than this.

19:26.720 --> 19:28.450
Tonight's buffet was great.

19:28.450 --> 19:29.750
I wanna try some.

19:29.750 --> 19:31.320
Then try some.

19:31.320 --> 19:33.730
I don't wanna go.

19:33.730 --> 19:37.850
Can you bring me dinner, mister?

19:38.350 --> 19:39.960
I guess that's okay.

19:42.360 --> 19:44.670
It's a promise.

19:51.870 --> 19:54.880
ASTRAL Second Day: Morning

19:53.110 --> 19:58.140
<i>Our team finally ran into 
a rival team on the second day.</i>

19:59.130 --> 20:02.710
I'm Ibara Academy's leader, Yuikawa Kanade.

20:03.150 --> 20:05.220
I want to form an alliance with you.

20:05.490 --> 20:06.720
An alliance?

20:06.720 --> 20:11.580
To be honest, we would be perfectly 
satisfied just making the top five.

20:11.580 --> 20:14.100
We don't really want 
to get into any trouble.

20:14.580 --> 20:16.860
You saw the Temporary 
Alliance command, right?

20:17.190 --> 20:21.590
It's an agreement to not 
invade each other's areas.

20:21.590 --> 20:24.170
You can also decide on 
a penalty if someone breaks it.

20:24.170 --> 20:24.930
Huh?

20:26.080 --> 20:28.410
<i>What's this guy planning?</i>

20:31.870 --> 20:33.120
Mya-chan?

20:33.120 --> 20:34.530
Asamiya-sama?

20:34.530 --> 20:36.650
Nanase! What did you do?!

20:36.650 --> 20:40.230
Oh, uh... it's because he...

20:40.880 --> 20:42.830
Ah, no time to explain!

20:43.950 --> 20:44.880
Wait!

20:45.150 --> 20:48.900
Well, that's a shame. 
Negotiations have broken down, I'd say.

20:49.940 --> 20:53.090
Shinohara, I'm going to join Nanase.

20:53.090 --> 20:55.120
Nanase! Don't just attack blindly!

20:55.120 --> 20:56.350
I know already!

20:56.350 --> 20:58.100
Do you want to be killed by my attacks?

20:58.100 --> 21:00.590
Just aim 'em so you don't hit me!

21:05.630 --> 21:07.960
Why did you do that, Nanase?

21:08.260 --> 21:10.260
Because that guy...

21:10.260 --> 21:14.200
Huh? Well, ultimately, 
we did beat Ibara Academy.

21:14.200 --> 21:15.970
But did you weigh up the odds?

21:15.970 --> 21:19.380
Who protected you when you charged 
into an enemy area with no plan?

21:19.380 --> 21:21.450
Hey, Enomoto. That's enough.

21:21.450 --> 21:23.160
It was the same last year.

21:23.620 --> 21:27.170
We kept tripping over each other 
and an inferior team finally got us.

21:27.570 --> 21:29.220
We aren't here for fun!

21:29.220 --> 21:32.460
If we have to deal with your stupidity, 
it'll be an issue for everyone!

21:32.750 --> 21:35.980
Why? I thought...

21:35.980 --> 21:37.950
Huh? Speak up, will you—

21:37.950 --> 21:39.230
Shut up!

21:39.230 --> 21:41.880
Stupid Shinji! Don't talk to me <i>ever</i> again!

21:41.880 --> 21:42.850
Hey!

21:43.450 --> 21:44.590
Mya-chan!

21:44.590 --> 21:45.450
Asamiya-sama!

21:47.550 --> 21:48.690
Shinohara.

21:49.250 --> 21:51.340
Am I the bad guy here?

21:51.340 --> 21:53.520
Well, I don't think you're wrong,

21:53.520 --> 21:56.630
but I'm not sure if that was the right move.

21:57.190 --> 21:57.960
I see.

21:59.290 --> 22:02.950
<i>Our teamwork's a mess. What do I do?</i>

22:02.960 --> 22:04.470
Second Day: Finished

22:04.470 --> 22:05.970
Team with the most held areas:
 District 3's Ouka Academy

22:04.470 --> 22:05.970
spaces

22:05.970 --> 22:07.470
Team with the most supporting votes:
 District 4's Eimei Academy

22:07.470 --> 22:09.970
Eimei Academy's
collected resources:

22:07.470 --> 22:09.970
bases

22:07.470 --> 22:09.970
Areas held:
